<CONTENT>I can’t answer this precisely from the evidence provided because none of the retrieved documents is the City of Hartford Municipal Employees’ Retirement Fund (MERF) general investment consultant RFP.

What the evidence actually contains:
- Texas Municipal Retirement System (TMRS) — Non-Discretionary General Investment Consulting Services RFP
- San Diego City Employees’ Retirement System (SDCERS) — General Investment Consultant RFP
- City of Madison Police Officers’ & Firefighters’ Retirement System — Investment Consulting Services RFP
- Police Retirement System of St. Louis — Actuarial Auditing Services RFP
- Missouri LAGERS — Private Market Consulting Services RFP

Because your question asks for “all the minimum requirements” in the City of Hartford MERF RFP, using these other entities’ RFPs would risk giving you incorrect information.

The only explicit “minimum requirements” section for a general investment consultant in the evidence is from TMRS, and those requirements are entity-specific, not Hartford MERF’s. For clarity, TMRS required that a respondent:
1. Currently provide non-discretionary general investment advice to at least 5 public pension plans larger than $5 billion and at least 2 public plans over $20 billion.
2. Certify in writing that it will act as a fiduciary.
3. Accept a contractual negligence standard, not just gross negligence.
4. Agree to the Prudent Expert standard.
5. Agree to Texas law and venue.
6. Be SEC-registered under the Investment Advisers Act of 1940 and submit Form ADV Parts 1 and 2.
7. Hold all required legal authorizations, permits, licenses, and certifications.
8. Have no actual or potential material conflict with the board, staff, or custodian.
9. Have fiduciary and liability insurance.
10. Be willing to enter into an agreement substantially similar to the draft agreement in the RFP.
11. Certify that it has and will maintain adequate controls and operational support.

But again, that is TMRS, not Hartford MERF.

If you want, send the Hartford MERF RFP or its minimum qualifications section, and I can extract every proposer requirement exactly and organize them cleanly.
